{"step_index":2570,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T05:14:34Z","thinking":"**Constructing the Benchmark Harness**\n\nI'm now diving into the implementation of the `sovra_true_full_stream.c` benchmark harness. My focus is on ensuring each worker thread computes its precise section of the entire vector matrix, following the specified partitioning strategy: `start_node = t * (...)`. I'm aiming for a bare-metal, full-stream approach to accurately gauge performance.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// SOVRA True Full-Stream Bare-Metal Memory Benchmark (Zero Sample-Cap Shortcuts)\\n// Substrate: Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (16 GB Physical LPDDR5X RAM, 10 Cores)\\n// Purpose: Stream through EVERY SINGLE FLOAT in the vector matrix to prove true physical DRAM throughput.\\n\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <stdbool.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <fcntl.h>\\n#include <unistd.h>\\n#include <sys/mman.h>\\n#include <sys/stat.h>\\n#include <sys/resource.h>\\n#include <pthread.h>\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n#include <mach/mach_time.h>\\n\\n#define DIM 18432\\n#define NUM_CORES 10\\n\\nstatic volatile double g_volatile_sink = 0.0;\\n\\nstatic double get_time_sec(void) {\\n    static mach_timebase_info_data_t timebase;\\n    if (timebase.denom == 0) {\\n        mach_timebase_info(&timebase);\\n    }\\n    uint64_t time = mach_absolute_time();\\n    return (double)time * timebase.numer / timebase.denom / 1e9;\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline float sovra_18432d_dot_neon(const float *a, const float *b) {\\n    float32x4_t acc0 = vdupq_n_f32(0.0f);\\n    float32x4_t acc1 = vdupq_n_f32(0.0f);\\n\\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < DIM; i += 8) {\\n        float32x4_t va0 = vld1q_f32(a + i);\\n        float32x4_t vb0 = vld1q_f32(b + i);\\n        acc0 = vmlaq_f32(acc0, va0, vb0);\\n\\n        float32x4_t va1 = vld1q_f32(a + i + 4);\\n        float32x4_t vb1 = vld1q_f32(b + i + 4);\\n        acc1 = vmlaq_f32(acc1, va1, vb1);\\n    }\\n    float32x4_t sum = vaddq_f32(acc0, acc1);\\n    return vaddvq_f32(sum);\\n}\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    const float *query;\\n    const float *matrix;\\n    size_t start_node;\\n    size_t node_count;\\n    double local_sum;\\n} WorkerTask;\\n\\nstatic void *full_stream_worker(void *arg) {\\n    WorkerTask *task = (WorkerTask *)arg;\\n    double sum = 0.0;\\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < task->node_count; i++) {\\n        size_t node_idx = task->start_node + i;\\n        const float *target = task->matrix + (node_idx * DIM);\\n        float dot = sovra_18432d_dot_neon(task->query, target);\\n        sum += dot\n<truncated 4762 bytes>","Description":"\"True Full-Stream Bare-Metal Benchmark streaming through 100% of memory.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/multilang_benchmark/sovra_true_full_stream.c\"","toolAction":"\"Writing True Full Stream benchmark C source\"","toolSummary":"\"Write True Full Stream C code\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
